(*
# Probe
Prelude for short scripts that inspect a running client headless, without
opening Simba. It's meant for external tools such as LLM agents.

Probes include WaspLib with `WL_READ_ONLY`, so they never send input to the
client and can run while a script is botting on it.

Write the snippet to `Agents/probes/<name>.simba`:
```pascal
{$I WaspLib/tools/agents/probe.simba}
begin
  WriteLn Inventory.Slots.Count();
  TAgent.Save(Target.GetImage(), 'client');
end.
```
Then run it against the client handle printed by `tools/agents/find_client.simba`:
```
Simba --target=<handle> --run Agents/probes/<name>.simba
```
*)
{$DEFINE WL_READ_ONLY}
{$I WaspLib/main.simba}
{$I WaspLib/tools/agents/agent.simba}
